    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I can't dump the whole roadmap doc here right now, but the gist is we're moving away from a single central hub to a distributed system with 50 localized nodes. Each node will handle its own regional logistics, inventory, and routing, rather than having you manage the global sync. I'm worried about \"single point of failure\" risks with you being the only central brain. Just start with a preliminary simulation based on what you know about the current scale vs. a distributed model.",
